1
00:00:19,393 --> 00:00:22,230
- Where have you been?
- Hunting and gathering.

2
00:00:22,730 --> 00:00:26,192
The victim's name is Timothy Hartley.
He was killed sometime last night.

3
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,528
He was shot in the chest,
and then his throat was slit.

4
00:00:28,694 --> 00:00:29,737
Charming.

5
00:00:29,862 --> 00:00:32,281
His I.D. says he's from about a hundred
miles away from here... Hillsborough.

6
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:33,991
No sign of what he was doing up here.

7
00:00:34,158 --> 00:00:35,409
Sheriff says Hartley's car's down the road.

8
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:36,577
- I'll check it out.
- All right.

9
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:38,746
- You tell him?
- Tell him what?

10
00:00:39,455 --> 00:00:42,416
- Coroner's office sent Steiner.
- Dr. Steiner?

11
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:47,255
And we all know how much you like
to make fun of Dr. Steiner so don't, okay?

12
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:48,464
I don't know what you're talking about.

13
00:00:48,589 --> 00:00:51,008
- No humoring yourself at his expense.
- Is he that way?

14
00:00:53,177 --> 00:00:54,637
Top of the morning to you, Steiner.

15
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:58,558
- You're looking trim.
- Jane.

16
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:05,648
Curiously considerate killer.

17
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:08,442
Slit his throat after the shots
to put him out of his misery.

18
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:11,737
- Three steps back, please.
- What?

19
00:01:12,154 --> 00:01:15,116
Please maintain a distance
of at least three steps from the body.

20
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:18,995
- Why?
- Because this body is a no-Jane zone.

21
00:01:19,662 --> 00:01:21,289
It will not be a playground for you.

22
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:24,917
You will not touch it or sniff it
or place playing cards on it

23
00:01:25,042 --> 00:01:26,752
or borrow it for an interrogation.

24
00:01:26,877 --> 00:01:30,214
If you do, a deputy will remove you.
Clear?

25
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:34,260
That's a little harsh, no?

26
00:01:34,927 --> 00:01:36,762
You have driven me
to desperate measures.

27
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:41,142
Well, I'm nothing if I'm not respectful
of my fellow crime-fighters.

28
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:43,269
But I can see everything I need to
from here anyway.

29
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:46,314
Really? W...

30
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:48,566
What exactly do you see?

31
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:52,236
He's in money, but not a banker
something more aggressive...

32
00:01:52,361 --> 00:01:54,864
stocks or such, social drinker

33
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:58,409
increased his intake lately
so under some pressure.

34
00:01:58,701 --> 00:02:01,996
A registered, uh, independent, though
always votes republican

35
00:02:02,163 --> 00:02:04,915
and as much money as he has,
his wife has more.

36
00:02:05,791 --> 00:02:08,586
- Ridiculous.
- He chose the tasteless tasseled loafers.

37
00:02:08,836 --> 00:02:12,048
She bought the opal-enlaced
sterling silver cuff links.

38
00:02:12,798 --> 00:02:13,841
Guesses.

39
00:02:14,258 --> 00:02:16,969
You might as well say he's going
to meet a tall, dark stranger.

40
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:20,306
That's very unlikely, doctor.
He's dead.

41
00:02:21,974 --> 00:02:24,727
And by the way, it looks like there's
something in his left-front pant pocket.

42
00:02:33,611 --> 00:02:36,447
You are about to think,
"What the hell"? "How did Jane..."

43
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:38,532
"Do that?"

44
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:43,829
How did you do that?

45
00:02:45,915 --> 00:02:48,668
"There are more things in
heaven and earth, Horatio"

46
00:02:49,293 --> 00:02:51,629
"than dreamt of in your philosophy."

47
00:02:55,424 --> 00:02:56,467
Okay. You planned ahead.

48
00:02:57,051 --> 00:02:58,678
You asked one of the sheriff's
deputies to call you

49
00:02:58,844 --> 00:03:00,638
the next time Steiner was on a case

50
00:03:00,846 --> 00:03:02,848
and then you asked them
to plant the note.

51
00:03:02,973 --> 00:03:04,433
That is an absurd theory.

52
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:06,686
You know this means another apology
at the coroner's office.

53
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:08,270
- No, it doesn't.
- Yes, it does.

54
00:03:08,437 --> 00:03:10,690
- Steiner loves the attention.
- Lisbon.

55
00:03:13,067 --> 00:03:14,110
What happened?

56
00:03:14,235 --> 00:03:15,277
Where are they?

57
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:21,742
It was a robbery.

58
00:03:21,867 --> 00:03:24,078
Two guys in a pickup pulled
the coroner's van over and held it up.

59
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:25,246
What'd they steal?

60
00:03:25,371 --> 00:03:27,039
- Get this... your vic's body.
- Hartley's corpse?

61
00:03:27,164 --> 00:03:29,333
That's right. Steiner tried to stop them
believe it or not.

62
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,670
- Dr. Steiner.
- Agent Lisbon.

63
00:03:33,921 --> 00:03:35,089
It's not as bad as it looks.

64
00:03:35,464 --> 00:03:37,883
Go get yourself checked out
and then come talk to us.

65
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:40,010
Jane, was this you?

66
00:03:40,302 --> 00:03:41,345
- W...
- Another trick?

67
00:03:42,722 --> 00:03:45,099
Jane had nothing to do
with this, nothing at all.

68
00:03:47,810 --> 00:03:49,729
- You didn't, did you?
- Of course not.

69
00:03:49,937 --> 00:03:52,273
- Swear on your life?
- On your life, even.

70
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:54,942
- Damn it. Who steals a body?
- Interesting though.

71
00:04:10,122 --> 00:04:12,583
The pickup was... pulled over.

72
00:04:13,125 --> 00:04:15,294
There were two men,
apparently working on the engine.

73
00:04:16,003 --> 00:04:17,254
They flagged us down

74
00:04:17,671 --> 00:04:20,632
{\an8}for help, we thought,
and then they pulled out guns.

75
00:04:21,049 --> 00:04:22,092
{\an8}Can you describe them?

76
00:04:22,843 --> 00:04:26,638
{\an8}They were both white
a little under 6 feet, I think.

77
00:04:26,764 --> 00:04:28,557
{\an8}I can't really say much more.

78
00:04:28,682 --> 00:04:31,268
{\an8}They wore hooded s...
jackets and sunglasses.

79
00:04:31,727 --> 00:04:34,521
{\an8}One went to the van
and dragged the body bag out.

80
00:04:35,522 --> 00:04:37,566
{\an8}The one guarding us
went to help him, and...

81
00:04:38,442 --> 00:04:39,485
That's when I...

82
00:04:40,402 --> 00:04:41,445
{\an8}Intervened.

83
00:04:41,612 --> 00:04:42,654
{\an8}Foolish.

84
00:04:42,863 --> 00:04:44,031
For once, I agree with you.

85
00:04:45,449 --> 00:04:48,202
{\an8}They put the body into the truck
and they... they took off.

86
00:04:48,327 --> 00:04:51,079
{\an8}- Why would anyone do this?
- We don't know yet. It's early.

87
00:04:53,999 --> 00:04:57,252
{\an8}I have to take this. I'm sorry.
Thank you for your time, Dr. Steiner.

88
00:04:57,711 --> 00:04:58,754
{\an8}Of course.

89
00:04:59,087 --> 00:05:01,840
{\an8}Lisbon. Thanks for getting back to me.

90
00:05:02,925 --> 00:05:05,928
{\an8}- Bye again, Mr. Jane.
- It wasn't your fault.

91
00:05:06,261 --> 00:05:07,304
{\an8}Excuse me?

92
00:05:08,222 --> 00:05:09,264
{\an8}They had guns.

93
00:05:09,681 --> 00:05:11,683
Big, scary guns.
There's nothing you could do.

94
00:05:13,477 --> 00:05:16,396
{\an8}The body is my responsibility,
my reason for being here.

95
00:05:17,189 --> 00:05:19,024
{\an8}Now I have no reason
or responsibility.

96
00:05:19,191 --> 00:05:20,317
There's nothing for me to do.

97
00:05:20,609 --> 00:05:23,904
{\an8}I don't expect you to understand why that
feels like failure to me but it does.

98
00:05:24,738 --> 00:05:27,199
{\an8}- Want a cup of tea?
- I don't think so.

99
00:05:29,701 --> 00:05:30,744
{\an8}Suit yourself.

100
00:05:31,578 --> 00:05:33,288
{\an8}I like the chapel in Yountville.

101
00:05:33,413 --> 00:05:36,083
{\an8}It's just a long way
for the guests to go.

102
00:05:36,375 --> 00:05:38,460
{\an8}What did you find out
about Vandermeer State Park?

103
00:05:38,836 --> 00:05:40,379
{\an8}I love that place.

104
00:05:43,549 --> 00:05:44,591
I see.

105
00:05:45,342 --> 00:05:47,135
{\an8}Well, I guess we'll just keep looking.

106
00:05:47,719 --> 00:05:49,680
I love you Craig. Bye.

107
00:05:50,848 --> 00:05:53,267
{\an8}Vandermeer State Park...
Beautiful for a wedding.

108
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,643
{\an8}I've hiked there.

109
00:05:54,768 --> 00:05:57,980
{\an8}There's an old quaker meeting house.
Oh, it would be perfect.

110
00:05:58,438 --> 00:06:01,775
But I guess they don't allow weddings.
It's too hard on the ground vegetation.

111
00:06:01,942 --> 00:06:03,235
What do we have on Hartley?

112
00:06:03,819 --> 00:06:05,654
Jane was right.
He was in finance.

113
00:06:05,821 --> 00:06:08,407
Ran a hedge fund called
the H.V. Wilder Fund.

114
00:06:08,699 --> 00:06:10,075
But his wife's family has the real money.

115
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,910
- Name's Cook.
- The Cooks?

116
00:06:12,244 --> 00:06:14,204
Yeah, I guess.
Wife's name is Peregrine.

117
00:06:14,454 --> 00:06:15,497
I'll deal with the family.

118
00:06:15,622 --> 00:06:17,207
You go and talk to the people
he worked with.

119
00:06:18,166 --> 00:06:19,501
Anything on the missing corpse?

120
00:06:19,626 --> 00:06:21,378
Forensics found no usable prints
on the van

121
00:06:21,503 --> 00:06:23,130
and nothing from the tire tracks
at the scene.

122
00:06:23,255 --> 00:06:25,173
Why steal a dead body?
What can they use it for?

123
00:06:25,507 --> 00:06:26,550
Got me.

124
00:06:27,009 --> 00:06:29,469
Go and have another talk with the two guys
that were with Steiner.

125
00:06:29,595 --> 00:06:31,722
Get any details
on the thieves or the truck.

126
00:06:31,972 --> 00:06:36,310
Van Pelt, look for any similar crimes
bodies that were stolen from hospitals

127
00:06:36,435 --> 00:06:38,520
- ambulances, anything.
- Good luck with the Cooks.

128
00:06:39,104 --> 00:06:41,440
Yeah, nothing like telling people
their loved ones are dead

129
00:06:41,565 --> 00:06:44,192
and oh, by the way,
we lost the corpse.

130
00:06:48,030 --> 00:06:50,532
None of this makes any sense.

131
00:06:52,451 --> 00:06:53,869
The last time I-I spoke to Tim

132
00:06:53,994 --> 00:06:56,705
he was telling me some stupid joke
he heard at work

133
00:06:57,289 --> 00:06:58,415
happy as ever.

134
00:06:59,625 --> 00:07:03,003
Who's responsible, agent?
My son-in-law didn't just disappear.

135
00:07:03,128 --> 00:07:04,755
Someone is accountable. Who?

136
00:07:04,963 --> 00:07:07,215
Ma'am, we don't know yet.
We're doing the best we can.

137
00:07:07,466 --> 00:07:09,343
- Not good enough.
- Mother!

138
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:11,762
My dear, when they tell you
they're doing their very best

139
00:07:11,887 --> 00:07:14,806
- that's exactly what they aren't doing.
- Hell of a place you've got here.

140
00:07:15,349 --> 00:07:17,476
- Where'd you get the money for it?
- Excuse me?

141
00:07:17,976 --> 00:07:21,063
The moolah. The scratch.
The shekels. The dollarinis.

142
00:07:21,313 --> 00:07:22,731
What does that have
to do with anything?

143
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:25,192
Obviously something
you're embarrassed about.

144
00:07:27,110 --> 00:07:28,946
- Sugar beets.
- Sugar beets?

145
00:07:29,446 --> 00:07:32,199
- My, uh, my grandfather grew them.
- I love sugar beets.

146
00:07:32,866 --> 00:07:34,868
There's no shame in sugar beets, Elspeth.

147
00:07:35,827 --> 00:07:39,122
Mrs. Hartley, we found your husband's body
a hundred miles from here.

148
00:07:39,247 --> 00:07:43,126
- Any idea what he was doing out there?
- No, none at all.

149
00:07:43,543 --> 00:07:46,630
Was there anything out of the ordinary
going on in his life? Troubles at work?

150
00:07:46,838 --> 00:07:49,174
- Changes in his schedule?
- No.

151
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:53,178
We started...
Talking about having...

152
00:07:54,554 --> 00:07:55,597
A family...

153
00:07:56,223 --> 00:07:57,265
A while back.

154
00:08:00,978 --> 00:08:02,020
There, there, dear.

155
00:08:03,313 --> 00:08:04,731
If there are no more questions...

156
00:08:04,856 --> 00:08:06,566
You didn't like your
son-in-law, did you?

157
00:08:07,275 --> 00:08:10,862
You found him vulgar
despite his highfalutin job.

158
00:08:11,071 --> 00:08:14,032
And you... you're frightened.

159
00:08:14,992 --> 00:08:19,287
The body's disappearance alarms you
in a very specific way. What is that?

160
00:08:19,538 --> 00:08:22,916
Harrison, please show our visitors out.

161
00:08:27,295 --> 00:08:29,172
Thank you. I'm good.

162
00:08:31,967 --> 00:08:33,010
{\an8}"Oh, God."

163
00:08:33,552 --> 00:08:34,970
Why do these things happen?

164
00:08:36,805 --> 00:08:38,348
How long have you and
Mr. Hartley been partners?

165
00:08:38,515 --> 00:08:40,934
Oh, uh, five years or so.

166
00:08:41,977 --> 00:08:43,228
We were both interested in a fund

167
00:08:43,353 --> 00:08:45,981
that offered slightly esoteric
financial instruments.

168
00:08:46,356 --> 00:08:48,650
- A hedge fund.
- What we do is pretty complicated.

169
00:08:48,775 --> 00:08:50,068
I don't want to bore you
with the details.

170
00:08:50,193 --> 00:08:53,155
As I understand it, you rely on a strategy
that exploits mean reversion tendencies

171
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:55,323
of crosscurrent far forward rates.
Is that right?

172
00:08:55,741 --> 00:08:56,783
Yes.

173
00:08:57,534 --> 00:08:58,994
What did Mr. Hartley
do for the fund?

174
00:08:59,369 --> 00:09:01,538
Built it.
Designed the strategy.

175
00:09:01,705 --> 00:09:03,874
Certifiable genius.
The best.

176
00:09:04,082 --> 00:09:05,876
A fund like yours can lose
people a lot of money.

177
00:09:07,210 --> 00:09:09,337
- Any angry investors?
- No, no, no.

178
00:09:09,755 --> 00:09:11,631
Recently, we've had excellent returns.

179
00:09:11,923 --> 00:09:14,801
What about work?
Did Hartley have problems here?

180
00:09:15,552 --> 00:09:16,887
"Loved" is the word.

181
00:09:17,095 --> 00:09:19,848
- How about trouble at home?
- No. Tim adored Peregrine.

182
00:09:19,973 --> 00:09:21,767
He... he... he was a boy scout.

183
00:09:21,892 --> 00:09:23,852
He would never play around,
wouldn't even think of it.

184
00:09:23,977 --> 00:09:28,190
- He's a straight... straight arrow.
- I see.

185
00:09:28,523 --> 00:09:29,566
The straightest.

186
00:09:32,444 --> 00:09:33,904
So nothing new from
the guys with Steiner

187
00:09:34,029 --> 00:09:37,074
but it wasn't an entirely
wasted journey. I got scones.

188
00:09:37,783 --> 00:09:38,825
I found something.

189
00:09:39,117 --> 00:09:42,037
Three other corpses have been stolen
from vehicles leaving crime scenes

190
00:09:42,162 --> 00:09:43,205
over the past six months.

191
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:45,165
- Who caught the cases?
- We did.

192
00:09:45,707 --> 00:09:47,000
- Rigsby.
- O'Laughlin.

193
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:48,293
Why is the FBI on this?

194
00:09:48,418 --> 00:09:50,378
It's interstate. One of the corpses
was taken in Nevada.

195
00:09:50,504 --> 00:09:51,755
- You guys have a theory?
- Yeah.

196
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:53,548
We think the bodies are
being sold at tissue banks.

197
00:09:53,673 --> 00:09:54,716
Tissue banks?

198
00:09:54,841 --> 00:09:56,259
They harvest bone and tissue
from the corpses

199
00:09:56,384 --> 00:09:58,011
then sell them to
medical supply houses.

200
00:09:58,136 --> 00:10:00,472
You're supposed to get permission
from the family to sell the corpse

201
00:10:00,597 --> 00:10:01,932
but these guys are skipping that part.

202
00:10:02,099 --> 00:10:03,141
And tissue banks are regulated

203
00:10:03,266 --> 00:10:05,060
so more likely the thieves are
working with the Funeral Home.

204
00:10:05,227 --> 00:10:06,686
They provide the
bodies to tissue banks.

205
00:10:06,812 --> 00:10:08,605
I put together a list of
Funeral Homes in the area.

206
00:10:08,730 --> 00:10:10,315
- We can start with that.
- Great, yeah.

207
00:10:11,358 --> 00:10:14,194
Hey, Rigsby, my boss
asked me to come

208
00:10:14,528 --> 00:10:16,279
you know, since I've worked
with CBI before.

209
00:10:17,322 --> 00:10:19,199
I'm not trying to get in your face
is all I'm saying.

210
00:10:19,366 --> 00:10:20,408
Didn't think you were.

211
00:10:20,617 --> 00:10:22,077
- Okay, good.
- Okay.

212
00:10:29,876 --> 00:10:31,253
Dr. Steiner, I presume.

213
00:10:32,712 --> 00:10:33,797
What brings you back?

214
00:10:35,423 --> 00:10:36,508
Good news, actually.

215
00:10:37,092 --> 00:10:38,718
A small amount of blood
was recovered

216
00:10:38,844 --> 00:10:41,346
from the dirt under the body
at the crime scene.

217
00:10:42,013 --> 00:10:44,349
It contains two distinct
DNA signatures.

218
00:10:44,683 --> 00:10:45,976
The killer got cut, too.

219
00:10:46,309 --> 00:10:49,312
Yes, probably while using
a knife on the victim.

220
00:10:50,188 --> 00:10:53,775
There's not enough blood for an I.D.
but there could be more on the corpse.

221
00:10:54,067 --> 00:10:58,488
Interesting. Why did you come and tell
me that in person instead of calling?

222
00:10:58,697 --> 00:11:01,408
I would like to assist in some
small way, if that's all right.

223
00:11:04,035 --> 00:11:06,454
Okay. Let's go get
you a gun, shall we?

224
00:11:09,583 --> 00:11:11,501
Kidding. Welcome. Come on.

225
00:11:13,628 --> 00:11:15,881
Look sharp, Lisbon.
We have a visitor.

226
00:11:19,718 --> 00:11:23,180
- Dr. Steiner? Can I help you?
- Well, actually, I...

227
00:11:23,305 --> 00:11:25,098
Steiner's gonna be
joining us for a while.

228
00:11:25,599 --> 00:11:27,642
Um... okay.

229
00:11:27,767 --> 00:11:31,563
- What is all this mess?
- It's Hartley's calendar and phone records.

230
00:11:31,855 --> 00:11:33,899
We're making a list of people he saw
before he died.

231
00:11:34,065 --> 00:11:35,609
Meh. Clerical work.

232
00:11:36,151 --> 00:11:38,320
We need to figure out what the big secret is.

233
00:11:38,904 --> 00:11:40,822
- What big secret?
- Yeah, what big secret?

234
00:11:41,239 --> 00:11:43,909
The big, weird secret that the widow
and the partner

235
00:11:44,034 --> 00:11:47,412
and everyone won't tell us about
because it's too shameful to mention.

236
00:11:47,537 --> 00:11:48,830
It's funny you should mention that.

237
00:11:48,955 --> 00:11:51,708
He... he did have an appointment
every week with no description.

238
00:11:52,083 --> 00:11:54,753
Thursdays, 2:15 to 3:30.
No name, no address.

239
00:11:54,878 --> 00:11:56,463
- Interesting.
- Clerical work, huh?

240
00:11:56,713 --> 00:11:58,048
- Touché.
- If I may

241
00:11:58,590 --> 00:12:00,675
his car's GPS
might have an address.

242
00:12:01,051 --> 00:12:04,387
- Yes, it might.
- See? Useful already.

243
00:12:07,515 --> 00:12:09,142
2729 Hillview Avenue.

244
00:12:09,851 --> 00:12:11,478
This is the address
in Hartley's GPS.

245
00:12:12,812 --> 00:12:15,315
Okay, what's the game with Steiner?

246
00:12:15,482 --> 00:12:17,484
- No game.
- What's he doing here, then?

247
00:12:17,692 --> 00:12:18,735
What are any of us doing here?

248
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,737
We don't bring guests
on investigations.

249
00:12:20,862 --> 00:12:23,031
Maybe we should.
A different mystery sleuth for each case.

250
00:12:23,156 --> 00:12:24,199
Well, if this is some gag
you're pulling...

251
00:12:24,324 --> 00:12:26,284
It's not. He asked if he could
come along and I said he could.

252
00:12:26,409 --> 00:12:27,452
All right? That's it.

253
00:12:27,577 --> 00:12:29,788
We're building bridges,
mending fences...

254
00:12:29,955 --> 00:12:30,997
Okay.

255
00:12:31,122 --> 00:12:32,540
Planting seeds...

256
00:12:33,083 --> 00:12:34,709
- Laying foundations.
- Okay.

257
00:12:34,834 --> 00:12:38,296
It's a medical building, G.P.'s,
dentists, but mostly shrinks.

258
00:12:38,630 --> 00:12:39,881
How do you know who to talk to?

259
00:12:40,006 --> 00:12:42,217
Any calls on his phone records
to this address?

260
00:12:42,342 --> 00:12:44,177
No, but we can check his bank records
for payments.

261
00:12:44,302 --> 00:12:47,347
Oh, we'd need a warrant for that.
I'd rather just start knocking on doors.

262
00:12:47,472 --> 00:12:49,474
Then we're gonna need more people.
You'll have to clear that with admin.

263
00:12:53,144 --> 00:12:55,188
Okay, everybody, outside! Outside!

264
00:12:55,313 --> 00:12:57,607
Come on! It's not a drill!

265
00:12:57,774 --> 00:12:59,943
- Oh, God, Jane. Why did you do that?
- Hustle it out. Hustle it out.

266
00:13:00,068 --> 00:13:01,319
That's the way.

267
00:13:03,989 --> 00:13:05,031
All of you.

268
00:13:08,326 --> 00:13:11,621
Hello, ladies and gentlemen. My name
is Patrick Jane. I'm with the CBI.

269
00:13:11,746 --> 00:13:14,582
We are looking for the doctor
who treated Timothy Hartley.

270
00:13:14,833 --> 00:13:17,669
I know you have a doctor/patient
confidentiality thing.

271
00:13:17,919 --> 00:13:20,171
Let's not worry about that right now.

272
00:13:20,672 --> 00:13:24,676
Would Timothy Hartley's doctor
please raise his or her hand?

273
00:13:24,968 --> 00:13:26,136
Raise it on up.

274
00:13:28,096 --> 00:13:29,139
I know it's one of you.

275
00:13:29,389 --> 00:13:31,266
Maybe to your right
maybe to your left.

276
00:13:31,516 --> 00:13:33,727
Up, up, up, up with your hand.
Bring it up.

277
00:13:34,686 --> 00:13:36,104
Okay, so no one has raised their hand.

278
00:13:36,229 --> 00:13:39,983
That doesn't matter
because I know that you, ma'am

279
00:13:40,608 --> 00:13:43,069
are the person who we seek.
Please come forward.

280
00:13:43,194 --> 00:13:45,613
Everyone else, thank you,
and back to your quackery.

281
00:13:48,491 --> 00:13:51,828
- What's your name, ma'am?
- Dr. Wendelyne McCormick.

282
00:13:52,412 --> 00:13:56,291
And I won't discuss my patients
or the fact that someone is my patient.

283
00:13:56,499 --> 00:13:58,793
We're investigating the murder
of Timothy Hartley.

284
00:13:58,918 --> 00:14:00,295
He was killed last night.

285
00:14:01,629 --> 00:14:02,672
Oh, God.

286
00:14:04,758 --> 00:14:05,800
All right.

287
00:14:07,761 --> 00:14:08,803
How did you know it was me?

288
00:14:08,928 --> 00:14:10,889
Everyone else was looking
around to see who it was

289
00:14:11,264 --> 00:14:13,141
but you weren't, because you knew.

290
00:14:15,477 --> 00:14:18,229
Great. The fire department.
I'll go talk to 'em.

291
00:14:19,689 --> 00:14:21,816
Tim had been in therapy
for about four months.

292
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:24,986
He'd had a traumatizing experience
that he wanted to work through.

293
00:14:25,111 --> 00:14:26,279
What kind of an experience?

294
00:14:28,073 --> 00:14:30,658
Agent, can I get some assurance
of discretion from you?

295
00:14:31,076 --> 00:14:33,703
It's a sensitive matter
to the people around him.

296
00:14:33,870 --> 00:14:36,623
- We can't promise anything.
- Very well.

297
00:14:37,957 --> 00:14:41,586
About five months ago
he had an abduction experience.

298
00:14:42,003 --> 00:14:43,046
Excuse me?

299
00:14:43,171 --> 00:14:46,383
He believed he was abducted
by extraterrestrial beings...

300
00:14:49,094 --> 00:14:53,098
Taken to their ship, examined
and released.

301
00:14:57,102 --> 00:14:58,395
Kidnapped by aliens.

302
00:14:59,938 --> 00:15:00,980
Cool.

303
00:15:05,942 --> 00:15:07,944
"I was being lifted by
the light, up and away."

304
00:15:08,069 --> 00:15:11,322
"I-I couldn't... couldn't do anything."

305
00:15:11,447 --> 00:15:14,367
"I was just being...
taken right to the ship."

306
00:15:14,575 --> 00:15:16,869
It happened when Hartley was driving home
from a trip to Reno.

307
00:15:17,495 --> 00:15:19,414
We found a couple of these videos
on his personal laptop

308
00:15:19,580 --> 00:15:21,290
some kind of diary of the event.

309
00:15:21,791 --> 00:15:23,334
"And once on the ship, there were..."

310
00:15:25,086 --> 00:15:26,671
"There were beings all around me"

311
00:15:27,797 --> 00:15:28,840
"small..."

312
00:15:29,424 --> 00:15:30,466
"small..."

313
00:15:30,842 --> 00:15:32,135
"just ash gray."

314
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:35,805
"And there were a little taller ones too...
they're the same color."

315
00:15:36,139 --> 00:15:37,432
"They were leaders, I think."

316
00:15:38,307 --> 00:15:39,976
"It just all feels so..."

317
00:15:42,645 --> 00:15:43,980
"It feels so concrete"

318
00:15:44,689 --> 00:15:46,065
"so real."

319
00:15:46,774 --> 00:15:50,236
- Crazy.
- He sounds sincere to me.

320
00:15:50,361 --> 00:15:53,239
- Sincerely cuckoo.
- I don't see any sign he's lying.

321
00:15:53,364 --> 00:15:56,451
It could be a dream that he experienced
during a hypnagogic state.

322
00:15:56,576 --> 00:15:58,953
That would make it true for him
but not objectively real.

323
00:15:59,078 --> 00:16:00,872
Exactly. I agree with him completely.

324
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,707
Thousands of people say
it's happened to them.

325
00:16:02,832 --> 00:16:04,625
They can't all be crazy or lying.

326
00:16:05,626 --> 00:16:07,670
I'm just saying you
should keep an open mind.

327
00:16:08,087 --> 00:16:10,465
- You can't prove there aren't aliens.
- That's true.

328
00:16:10,631 --> 00:16:13,801
Okay, the point is the wife
had to have known about this.

329
00:16:14,135 --> 00:16:15,636
- We need to talk to her again.
- Yeah.

330
00:16:15,803 --> 00:16:16,971
Where are we with the body hunt?

331
00:16:17,388 --> 00:16:19,140
We've identified eight funeral parlors

332
00:16:19,265 --> 00:16:21,726
that had extensive legitimate dealings
with tissue banks.

333
00:16:21,851 --> 00:16:22,894
We're gonna start with them.

334
00:16:23,019 --> 00:16:24,437
We're splitting the interviews
with O'Laughlin.

335
00:16:24,729 --> 00:16:26,314
- All right, let me know what you find.
- Okay.

336
00:16:27,398 --> 00:16:28,691
Watch the skies, Grace.

337
00:16:31,903 --> 00:16:34,655
Tim told me as soon as it happened.

338
00:16:34,947 --> 00:16:37,992
He said he met them
in a field outside Auburn.

339
00:16:38,159 --> 00:16:39,494
Where we found his body?

340
00:16:41,871 --> 00:16:44,207
He kept going back.
He couldn't tell me why.

341
00:16:44,332 --> 00:16:46,876
I mean, he knew it wasn't rational.

342
00:16:47,251 --> 00:16:48,878
Why didn't you tell us this before?

343
00:16:49,128 --> 00:16:51,672
I got a call from Art Vella

344
00:16:52,965 --> 00:16:54,008
Tim's partner.

345
00:16:54,342 --> 00:16:57,053
He told me not to mention it, begged me.

346
00:16:57,178 --> 00:17:00,014
He said it would be devastating
for the business.

347
00:17:00,181 --> 00:17:01,641
You believed your husband's
story, didn't you?

348
00:17:02,350 --> 00:17:04,936
That's why you were so scared
when the body disappeared.

349
00:17:05,144 --> 00:17:07,355
- You thought the aliens took him.
- Okay, okay.

350
00:17:08,648 --> 00:17:09,690
Listen to me.

351
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:13,277
My husband wasn't crazy.

352
00:17:14,237 --> 00:17:15,279
Okay?

353
00:17:15,738 --> 00:17:17,865
He wouldn't lie to me
about something like that.

354
00:17:18,241 --> 00:17:21,577
Rubbish! When someone tells you
something contrary to fact

355
00:17:21,702 --> 00:17:23,454
they are lying, full stop.

356
00:17:23,621 --> 00:17:25,206
Don't start, mother.

357
00:17:25,665 --> 00:17:29,669
Agents, my son-in-law was drunk
or drug-addled or both.

358
00:17:30,169 --> 00:17:32,922
As for this tabloid trash
about men from Mars...

359
00:17:33,339 --> 00:17:34,382
- Ladies.
- How can you say that?

360
00:17:34,507 --> 00:17:36,133
- Ridiculous. Just ridiculous!
- This is so like you, mother...

361
00:17:36,259 --> 00:17:38,010
I've never heard such twaddle
in my life...

362
00:17:38,135 --> 00:17:40,054
- so closed off and close-minded.
- And he said it with a straight face.

363
00:17:40,179 --> 00:17:43,391
- You honestly think...
- Ladies. Ladies, that's enough.

364
00:17:43,975 --> 00:17:45,601
Wait. What are you looking for?

365
00:17:46,727 --> 00:17:48,396
Ah, yes.

366
00:17:50,439 --> 00:17:51,857
You're a scotch man, right?

367
00:17:53,234 --> 00:17:56,112
Uh, yes. I...

368
00:18:05,329 --> 00:18:06,956
Oh, no, no. I-I shouldn't.

369
00:18:08,791 --> 00:18:09,834
You really should.

370
00:18:13,045 --> 00:18:14,088
Cheers.

371
00:18:20,678 --> 00:18:21,804
You know, don't you?

372
00:18:23,055 --> 00:18:25,224
- Excuse me?
- You know that I'm sick.

373
00:18:26,892 --> 00:18:28,936
Why would Patrick Jane, of all people

374
00:18:29,562 --> 00:18:31,230
invite me to a fancy house

375
00:18:32,148 --> 00:18:34,900
and put a first-rate scotch
in my hand if he didn't know?

376
00:18:35,234 --> 00:18:38,362
- You've lost some weight... 8 pounds.
- Yes.

377
00:18:40,239 --> 00:18:41,616
Your face is looking drawn.

378
00:18:42,116 --> 00:18:43,618
You're taking some
powerful medication.

379
00:18:43,743 --> 00:18:45,369
I can see it in the
pallor of your skin.

380
00:18:45,786 --> 00:18:46,829
Yes.

381
00:18:49,248 --> 00:18:50,291
I'm dying.

382
00:18:51,626 --> 00:18:52,668
I have a month...

383
00:18:53,461 --> 00:18:54,962
Most likely, maybe less.

384
00:18:58,799 --> 00:18:59,842
I'm sorry.

385
00:19:07,975 --> 00:19:09,352
Thank you for the distraction.

386
00:19:11,812 --> 00:19:13,356
Well, it's always good to...

387
00:19:13,939 --> 00:19:14,982
Keep busy.

388
00:19:16,442 --> 00:19:19,737
There's probably some, uh,
Havana cigars in that box there.

389
00:19:20,488 --> 00:19:22,114
No. No, no. I...

390
00:19:22,865 --> 00:19:23,908
I couldn't.

391
00:19:25,076 --> 00:19:26,118
Could I?

392
00:19:28,621 --> 00:19:30,289
Well, you're right.

393
00:19:33,167 --> 00:19:34,585
This is a good cigar.

394
00:19:43,094 --> 00:19:46,597
The only other time
that I had been in a room like this

395
00:19:47,598 --> 00:19:50,309
was to examine a man
who died accidentally

396
00:19:50,810 --> 00:19:53,104
in the middle of an autoerotic ritual.

397
00:19:53,562 --> 00:19:55,815
Well, I bet he died
with a smile on his face.

398
00:20:02,613 --> 00:20:03,656
Excuse me.

399
00:20:05,074 --> 00:20:06,117
Can I help you?

400
00:20:08,494 --> 00:20:09,620
Just leaving Harrison.

401
00:20:15,084 --> 00:20:17,044
Why did you tell Peregrine
Hartley to lie to us, sir?

402
00:20:18,921 --> 00:20:20,297
I didn't tell her to lie.

403
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:23,926
I asked Peregrine not to raise
certain relevant information.

404
00:20:27,054 --> 00:20:28,097
Why'd you do that?

405
00:20:29,348 --> 00:20:32,309
Tim was the brain.
I handled clients, administration.

406
00:20:32,435 --> 00:20:35,604
Tim was the brain.
It's all about confidence.

407
00:20:36,021 --> 00:20:38,482
If the investors hear about
alien probes and whatnot

408
00:20:38,607 --> 00:20:40,151
confidence goes right out the window.

409
00:20:40,401 --> 00:20:42,069
Then I assume you asked him
not to talk about this.

410
00:20:42,278 --> 00:20:43,320
Constantly.

411
00:20:43,696 --> 00:20:45,990
But Mr. Hartley was growing certain
his experiences were real.

412
00:20:46,699 --> 00:20:48,075
He must've wanted to talk about it.

413
00:20:49,535 --> 00:20:51,746
- We had some arguments about it.
- Bad arguments?

414
00:20:51,871 --> 00:20:55,666
I didn't kill Tim because he wanted
to go public with his cuckoo story.

415
00:20:56,375 --> 00:20:59,295
You need to talk to that UFO
fruitcake that Tim met.

416
00:20:59,462 --> 00:21:00,504
They're friends about a week

417
00:21:00,629 --> 00:21:02,006
and then Tim wanted nothing more
to do with him.

418
00:21:02,131 --> 00:21:04,175
I think he was trying to
squeeze some money out of Tim.

419
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:05,342
What's his name?

420
00:21:05,593 --> 00:21:08,304
Kirk. Can you believe that?

421
00:21:09,346 --> 00:21:11,015
Newsom Kirk.

422
00:21:12,558 --> 00:21:14,852
Is there any way
you can keep this quiet?

423
00:21:15,102 --> 00:21:18,439
- I doubt it.
- $2.8 billion in assets.

424
00:21:18,731 --> 00:21:20,941
We're going down
because my partner

425
00:21:21,066 --> 00:21:24,069
thought he was
kidnapped by little green men.

426
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:27,239
- Gray.
- What?

427
00:21:27,573 --> 00:21:29,283
The little men. They're gray.

428
00:21:30,117 --> 00:21:32,161
- Thanks for your time. Appreciate it.
- Thank you, bye.

429
00:21:33,037 --> 00:21:35,372
Two down, two to go.
Wanna grab some food?

430
00:21:35,498 --> 00:21:37,583
Oh, there's an errand I wanna run.
Give me half an hour. I'll catch up.

431
00:21:37,708 --> 00:21:39,460
- Where you going? I'll take you.
- You don't need to do that.

432
00:21:39,585 --> 00:21:42,421
- Oh, come on. How far is it?
- It's a little ways. It's okay.

433
00:21:43,088 --> 00:21:45,841
- It's a wedding thing.
- Oh, I see.

434
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:47,343
Why don't I drop you off?

435
00:21:47,468 --> 00:21:49,678
I'll grab something to eat
and then stay in the car, okay?

436
00:21:51,430 --> 00:21:52,473
Sure.

437
00:22:13,702 --> 00:22:14,745
Hello.

438
00:22:14,870 --> 00:22:16,914
"Hey, it's O'Laughlin. I tried Grace.
She didn't answer."

439
00:22:17,122 --> 00:22:19,416
- She's busy.
- "Where are you? I've got something."

440
00:22:20,042 --> 00:22:22,002
Gary Wineman, funeral director.

441
00:22:22,336 --> 00:22:24,672
Mentioned tissue banks,
and he got very nervous.

442
00:22:25,589 --> 00:22:28,092
Mr. Wineman, these are
my colleagues from CBI

443
00:22:28,259 --> 00:22:29,635
Agents Rigsby and Van Pelt.

444
00:22:30,219 --> 00:22:32,137
Did agent O'Laughlin mention
what this was about, sir?

445
00:22:32,847 --> 00:22:37,685
Uh, some... bodies have been stolen
that might have gone to a tissue bank?

446
00:22:37,935 --> 00:22:40,646
No, that's the FBI's investigation.
We're investigating a murder.

447
00:22:43,274 --> 00:22:44,817
You didn't say anything about that.

448
00:22:47,361 --> 00:22:50,656
- I certainly don't know anything about it.
- Well, I hope so, sir.

449
00:22:50,865 --> 00:22:54,285
A case like this, anyone connected to it...
Even remotely connected... is in big trouble.

450
00:22:54,702 --> 00:22:55,995
Best thing to protect yourself...

451
00:22:56,287 --> 00:22:58,330
be very clear about what you know
and what you've done.

452
00:23:00,749 --> 00:23:02,251
Oh, God. Uh, look...

453
00:23:04,795 --> 00:23:05,838
We...

454
00:23:05,963 --> 00:23:08,424
My wife had a baby girl

455
00:23:08,883 --> 00:23:10,676
and we needed a little extra cash

456
00:23:10,801 --> 00:23:14,847
so I started selling bodies
to tissue banks...

457
00:23:15,264 --> 00:23:18,225
All... all legitimate.
I got permission every time.

458
00:23:19,602 --> 00:23:24,231
But the banks always want more bodies
and my wife got pregnant again.

459
00:23:24,481 --> 00:23:29,236
- Look, who came to you?
- My cousin. Not a good person.

460
00:23:29,361 --> 00:23:31,113
He said that if we split the fee

461
00:23:31,697 --> 00:23:34,742
he could provide bodies,
no permission necessary.

462
00:23:35,492 --> 00:23:38,078
All I have to do was dummy up paperwork
giving them false names.

463
00:23:38,370 --> 00:23:39,580
Did he bring you a corpse today?

464
00:23:39,830 --> 00:23:42,333
No, no, no, no.
But I... he has done this before

465
00:23:42,458 --> 00:23:45,377
with other funeral homes.
His name is Owen Melling.

466
00:23:45,544 --> 00:23:47,755
- I-I-I had no I...
- Where is he now, sir?

467
00:23:49,506 --> 00:23:52,468
Melling's done time for assault,
armed robbery and truck hijacking.

468
00:23:52,718 --> 00:23:55,012
Did the truck jobs with a buddy
named Jim Matthews.

469
00:23:55,220 --> 00:23:58,265
Both are on parole. Melling owes 15 years,
Matthew has 12.

470
00:23:58,390 --> 00:24:00,392
And they know if they get picked up
they're violated back in.

471
00:24:00,559 --> 00:24:01,602
It's good times.

472
00:24:05,356 --> 00:24:06,398
Owen Melling?

473
00:24:07,358 --> 00:24:08,400
CBI.

474
00:24:09,109 --> 00:24:10,778
We need to talk to you about
a robbery this morning.

475
00:24:11,695 --> 00:24:13,113
Just wanna get some facts straight.

476
00:24:13,447 --> 00:24:14,865
Come down to the office,
and we can explain.

477
00:24:15,240 --> 00:24:17,117
Jim. Cops.

478
00:24:19,620 --> 00:24:21,288
- Jim Matthews?
- Yeah. What's up?

479
00:24:21,413 --> 00:24:23,415
Says it's about some
robbery this morning.

480
00:24:24,541 --> 00:24:25,584
So what?

481
00:24:25,793 --> 00:24:27,503
- We were right here.
- That's right.

482
00:24:27,795 --> 00:24:28,837
Been here all day.

483
00:24:28,963 --> 00:24:30,089
Yeah, well, we still
need to talk to you.

484
00:24:30,297 --> 00:24:31,382
Now get your hands
out of your pocket.

485
00:24:31,507 --> 00:24:34,093
- Hands where we can see 'em.
- You heard him. Now.

486
00:24:35,219 --> 00:24:37,262
Don't hassle my boy!
He ain't done nothin'!

487
00:24:37,429 --> 00:24:38,639
Put the weapon down, ma'am.

488
00:24:38,889 --> 00:24:41,475
You just wanna make more trouble for him.
I won't have it.

489
00:24:41,976 --> 00:24:44,478
We just wanna talk to your son.
Everything's gonna be fine.

490
00:24:44,895 --> 00:24:46,188
Just put down the gun, ma'am.

491
00:24:47,606 --> 00:24:48,649
Please!

492
00:24:53,195 --> 00:24:54,238
Gun!

493
00:25:19,888 --> 00:25:22,641
O'Llaughlin, Grace is in trouble.
Cover me.

494
00:25:27,187 --> 00:25:28,230
O'Laughlin!

495
00:25:30,315 --> 00:25:31,400
Grace, get down!

496
00:25:36,822 --> 00:25:39,366
On the ground! Face down! Now!

497
00:25:41,285 --> 00:25:42,369
Get on the ground!

498
00:25:52,127 --> 00:25:55,005
- How'd the interview with Matthews go?
- Didn't. He asked for a lawyer.

499
00:25:55,630 --> 00:25:58,258
- What'd you find in Melling's house?
- No sign of Hartley's body.

500
00:25:58,508 --> 00:26:00,052
Forensics is checking
the pickup for DNA.

501
00:26:00,218 --> 00:26:02,262
I got something.
According to his cell phone records

502
00:26:02,387 --> 00:26:05,223
Melling made a call yesterday
to a Wellview Funeral Home.

503
00:26:05,390 --> 00:26:06,641
Could be where they dropped off
Hartley's body.

504
00:26:06,850 --> 00:26:10,062
Get Steiner and go and check it out.
If the body's there he's the one to I.D. it.

505
00:26:10,187 --> 00:26:11,229
Sure.

506
00:26:11,354 --> 00:26:12,397
Tracked down an address
for Newsom Kirk

507
00:26:12,522 --> 00:26:13,607
the guy Hartley had
a falling-out with.

508
00:26:13,732 --> 00:26:16,568
He runs an organization for abductees
called the Fourth Kind Foundation.

509
00:26:16,818 --> 00:26:17,861
Office is downtown.

510
00:26:17,986 --> 00:26:19,529
- Does he have a sheet?
- Running it now.

511
00:26:20,030 --> 00:26:22,699
We'll go talk to him.
Call if anything pops. Okay.

512
00:26:27,621 --> 00:26:29,581
Newsom Kirk, I'm agent Lisbon.

513
00:26:29,706 --> 00:26:33,877
- This is agent Cho. We're with the CBI.
Yes. So sad about Hartley. Welcome.

514
00:26:34,795 --> 00:26:35,837
Welcome.

515
00:26:36,671 --> 00:26:39,216
Agent Cho, you... you've...
you've been, haven't you?

516
00:26:39,549 --> 00:26:40,592
Excuse me?

517
00:26:40,717 --> 00:26:43,261
Up. Taken, with them.

518
00:26:44,262 --> 00:26:45,305
No.

519
00:26:45,639 --> 00:26:47,891
Well, I'm getting a...
I'm getting a definite sense.

520
00:26:48,975 --> 00:26:53,063
It sometimes takes a person years
to realize they've had the experience.

521
00:26:53,230 --> 00:26:56,316
- Timothy Hartley.
- Of course. Sorry.

522
00:26:56,858 --> 00:26:58,735
You met him through
the foundation, right?

523
00:26:58,985 --> 00:27:00,987
Yeah. We're here to serve abductees

524
00:27:02,447 --> 00:27:05,117
help them come to terms
with their experience.

525
00:27:05,784 --> 00:27:06,827
Spread the word.

526
00:27:07,285 --> 00:27:08,995
Tim wanted to talk about
what he'd been going through.

527
00:27:09,162 --> 00:27:11,665
He asked us to keep it in confidence,
and... and we did.

528
00:27:11,832 --> 00:27:14,167
And that's all you did...
talk about his experience?

529
00:27:14,459 --> 00:27:17,546
No. As a matter of fact,
Tim had a lot of money.

530
00:27:18,380 --> 00:27:21,466
And frankly, we... we need money

531
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:24,261
we had... we had several
quite serious discussions

532
00:27:24,386 --> 00:27:26,638
about funding this... this place.

533
00:27:27,222 --> 00:27:28,265
As a child...

534
00:27:29,141 --> 00:27:31,184
Did... did you have, um, dreams

535
00:27:31,309 --> 00:27:33,019
where you were floating
through the house

536
00:27:33,145 --> 00:27:35,355
as though pulled by an unseen force?

537
00:27:36,106 --> 00:27:37,149
No.

538
00:27:38,483 --> 00:27:42,779
Uh, we heard that the, uh, two of you
had some sort of a falling-out?

539
00:27:43,113 --> 00:27:45,157
He decided that he wanted to
start his own foundation.

540
00:27:45,282 --> 00:27:47,909
- Uh, his right, I say.
- It never got angry?

541
00:27:48,034 --> 00:27:52,664
No, no. Uh, if you're looking
for someone Tim had a fight with

542
00:27:52,956 --> 00:27:54,541
you should talk to that shrink of his.

543
00:27:55,125 --> 00:27:57,377
Uh, McCormick.

544
00:27:58,003 --> 00:27:59,421
She wanted to write a book about him.

545
00:27:59,754 --> 00:28:02,257
He said no. She was angry.

546
00:28:02,382 --> 00:28:04,384
- Okay.
- Boss, from Rigsby.

547
00:28:05,719 --> 00:28:08,597
Mr. Newsom, is your real name
Garrett Rosten?

548
00:28:09,055 --> 00:28:11,558
And did you spend a year in Chino prison
for fraud?

549
00:28:12,309 --> 00:28:13,977
Because your arrest record
says you did.

550
00:28:15,854 --> 00:28:18,940
In my previous life,
I was Garrett Rosten, yes.

551
00:28:19,274 --> 00:28:22,319
Mr. Hartley seems like the kind of guy
who would research somebody

552
00:28:22,444 --> 00:28:24,070
If he was considering funding them.

553
00:28:24,321 --> 00:28:28,241
- Did he find out about this?
- I never hid Garrett.

554
00:28:28,909 --> 00:28:31,828
- I'm simply a different person now.
- Not that different.

555
00:28:32,037 --> 00:28:35,248
There's a bench warrant out for your arrest
for kiting checks.

556
00:28:35,957 --> 00:28:37,792
- We're gonna have to take you in.
- Turn around, please.

557
00:28:39,544 --> 00:28:42,797
It's... it's okay. It's...
Just a misunderstanding.

558
00:28:44,507 --> 00:28:45,550
Hey, agent.

559
00:28:45,884 --> 00:28:48,678
The important thing is that you
take a look inside yourself

560
00:28:49,387 --> 00:28:51,389
and start questioning
those experiences...

561
00:28:52,098 --> 00:28:53,141
that you can't explain.

562
00:28:53,642 --> 00:28:54,684
Never happened.

563
00:28:55,518 --> 00:28:56,561
I believe you.

564
00:28:59,689 --> 00:29:00,732
Wake up.

565
00:29:03,777 --> 00:29:06,613
Newsom Kirk posted bail.
He's gonna be gone in an hour.

566
00:29:06,821 --> 00:29:09,407
Just in time for the
6:10 to Alpha Centauri.

567
00:29:09,741 --> 00:29:11,868
He was right about
Hartley's psychiatrist.

568
00:29:12,077 --> 00:29:14,371
She did propose a book,
but she withdrew it.

569
00:29:14,663 --> 00:29:16,248
- So she had motive.
- Kinda.

570
00:29:16,581 --> 00:29:18,708
- Who do you think did it?
- Jabba the Hutt.

571
00:29:18,875 --> 00:29:20,919
- Seriously.
- Ming the merciless.

572
00:29:21,169 --> 00:29:22,545
- Okay.
- Alf?

573
00:29:23,213 --> 00:29:25,423
When the aliens do come,
I hope they eat you.

574
00:29:30,345 --> 00:29:32,347
- Lisbon.
- Theresa, Brenda Shettrick.

575
00:29:32,597 --> 00:29:35,600
A local news crew is about
to interview Dr. Steiner

576
00:29:35,725 --> 00:29:38,270
about the Hartley case.
Just thought you'd like to know.

577
00:29:38,770 --> 00:29:40,897
He's supposed to be looking
for Hartley's body.

578
00:29:41,231 --> 00:29:42,857
No, he's here.

579
00:29:43,024 --> 00:29:44,067
"What interview?"

580
00:29:44,276 --> 00:29:46,444
Some background on tissue banks
and the corpse trade.

581
00:29:46,569 --> 00:29:48,613
There's a lot of interest.
He offered to do it.

582
00:29:48,905 --> 00:29:51,574
- "You didn't know anything?"
- I'll be right there.

583
00:29:54,327 --> 00:29:55,370
Bye, Lisbon.

584
00:29:59,416 --> 00:30:00,959
The legitimate trade in tissue

585
00:30:01,084 --> 00:30:04,296
is a valuable source of biological material
for medical use.

586
00:30:04,629 --> 00:30:07,590
Unfortunately, this illegal trade
has halted the investigation

587
00:30:07,716 --> 00:30:10,010
- into the death of Timothy Hartley.
- How's that?

588
00:30:10,176 --> 00:30:12,679
Well, I-I just came
from a funeral home

589
00:30:12,846 --> 00:30:14,806
where we had hoped to find
Mr. Hartley's body

590
00:30:14,931 --> 00:30:18,268
and it's... it's... it's not there.
The thieves have hidden it somewhere.

591
00:30:18,893 --> 00:30:20,687
And there is crucial
evidence... blood evidence...

592
00:30:20,812 --> 00:30:23,940
on Mr. Hartley's body
that will identify the killers.

593
00:30:24,232 --> 00:30:26,234
- Brenda.
- If we don't find that evidence...

594
00:30:26,359 --> 00:30:28,820
- Now.
- Guys, that's it. Thanks very much.

595
00:30:29,362 --> 00:30:30,572
Did I do something wrong?

596
00:30:31,114 --> 00:30:32,907
We don't talk to the press
about evidence.

597
00:30:33,033 --> 00:30:35,118
It kinda tells the killer
what we're looking for.

598
00:30:35,410 --> 00:30:36,995
Oh. Sorry.

599
00:30:37,954 --> 00:30:39,831
- How did I do otherwise?
- Oh, good.

600
00:30:43,168 --> 00:30:45,003
- Hey, Cho.
- Yeah.

601
00:30:45,712 --> 00:30:47,756
I think O'Laughlin flaked
on Van Pelt yesterday.

602
00:30:49,507 --> 00:30:50,550
What do you mean?

603
00:30:50,675 --> 00:30:52,719
Well, he saw she was in trouble
and he didn't do anything.

604
00:30:53,094 --> 00:30:54,763
- Guess he was scared.
- It happens.

605
00:30:55,096 --> 00:30:56,139
Yeah.

606
00:30:56,765 --> 00:30:58,808
- Van Pelt doesn't know this?
- No.

607
00:30:59,809 --> 00:31:00,852
I don't know.

608
00:31:01,770 --> 00:31:03,104
The question is,
does she need to know?

609
00:31:03,938 --> 00:31:06,399
Yeah, it's tough.
Your call.

610
00:31:11,946 --> 00:31:16,159
Dr. Steiner, I'm the coroner.
You saw the news story on Hartley's body?

611
00:31:17,410 --> 00:31:20,246
Well, I lied. I did find the body.

612
00:31:21,039 --> 00:31:25,001
There is evidence on it
and it will convict you of murder.

613
00:31:26,294 --> 00:31:28,296
But I haven't given
the police the body.

614
00:31:28,421 --> 00:31:34,302
I've kept it, and I'm willing to sell it
along with my silence, for $50,000.

615
00:31:35,762 --> 00:31:37,013
Because I'm a dying man.

616
00:31:38,098 --> 00:31:40,392
All I want is a few days of real comfort
before I'm gone.

617
00:31:42,602 --> 00:31:45,230
Think about it.
You know how to reach me.

618
00:31:49,109 --> 00:31:50,151
How was that?

619
00:31:51,152 --> 00:31:52,195
Not bad.

620
00:31:52,695 --> 00:31:56,074
Little over-the-top
but, you know, credible, nonetheless.

621
00:31:56,783 --> 00:31:57,826
Sorry.

622
00:31:58,952 --> 00:32:01,955
- Still getting used to all this deception.
- What deception?

623
00:32:02,622 --> 00:32:04,541
You did find Hartley's body
at a funeral home.

624
00:32:04,874 --> 00:32:06,626
Yes, but there was no blood
evidence on it.

625
00:32:06,876 --> 00:32:10,046
You can't catch a fish without bait.

626
00:32:10,422 --> 00:32:12,882
We will tell agent Lisbon
what's going on, yes?

627
00:32:13,133 --> 00:32:16,177
- Oh, yeah, eventually.
- Agent Lisbon's a good person.

628
00:32:16,886 --> 00:32:18,012
She reminds me of...

629
00:32:19,848 --> 00:32:20,890
never mind.

630
00:32:21,349 --> 00:32:24,144
Showtime. Huh?
Let's go.

631
00:32:26,688 --> 00:32:27,730
Yes?

632
00:32:35,820 --> 00:32:37,238
Testing one, two.

633
00:32:37,363 --> 00:32:38,406
Testing two.

634
00:32:38,906 --> 00:32:40,241
"Testing one, two."

635
00:32:40,575 --> 00:32:44,245
Yes, Dr. Steiner.
We can hear you, just like before.

636
00:32:44,620 --> 00:32:45,663
I'm a little nervous.

637
00:32:45,788 --> 00:32:47,373
"You're doing a great job.
You look the part."

638
00:32:48,166 --> 00:32:49,208
Are you sure about this?

639
00:32:49,375 --> 00:32:51,627
Are you ever gonna tire
of asking me that?

640
00:32:51,919 --> 00:32:52,962
No.

641
00:32:56,257 --> 00:32:57,300
Someone's coming.

642
00:33:16,319 --> 00:33:17,361
Go.

643
00:33:19,614 --> 00:33:21,532
- Dr. Steiner?
- Put your hands where I can see 'em!

644
00:33:21,657 --> 00:33:23,326
- Hands! Hands in the air!
- I'm not armed.

645
00:33:23,451 --> 00:33:24,494
I'm... I'm not armed.
I'm not armed.

646
00:33:24,619 --> 00:33:26,579
It's the butler! It's the butler!
It's the butler!

647
00:33:26,704 --> 00:33:28,956
It's the but... the butler did it!
I always wanted to say that.

648
00:33:29,081 --> 00:33:30,333
But wait. It gets better.

649
00:33:31,792 --> 00:33:32,835
Let's go.

650
00:33:33,628 --> 00:33:38,216
Ms. Cook. Good evening. Remember
me? I can't hear anything with this.

651
00:33:38,341 --> 00:33:41,260
The good doctor here told us
that Timothy Hartley's murder

652
00:33:41,594 --> 00:33:43,346
cut himself whilst doing the killing.

653
00:33:43,471 --> 00:33:46,265
Yeah. Would you mind terribly
showing me your hand?

654
00:33:55,191 --> 00:33:56,901
You must let Harrison go.

655
00:33:57,235 --> 00:33:59,737
He has done nothing but serve me
faithfully and well.

656
00:34:00,071 --> 00:34:03,950
As I explained, ma'am our D.A. will
drop the charges against your Butler

657
00:34:04,617 --> 00:34:06,410
if you answer our questions honestly.

658
00:34:06,536 --> 00:34:09,121
I feel like I'm haggling in a
bazaar over the cost of a rug.

659
00:34:11,165 --> 00:34:15,628
But if you will release
Harrison, then I will speak.

660
00:34:15,878 --> 00:34:17,463
Your son-in-law was about to go public

661
00:34:17,588 --> 00:34:19,549
with the whole alien adventure
thing, wasn't he?

662
00:34:19,924 --> 00:34:21,008
More than that.

663
00:34:21,717 --> 00:34:24,595
He wanted to start a global foundation
for abductees

664
00:34:24,762 --> 00:34:27,306
to see to their needs
and promote their cause.

665
00:34:27,807 --> 00:34:30,101
He was gonna call it
The Cook Family Foundation.

666
00:34:30,935 --> 00:34:33,354
Well, that wasn't going to happen.

667
00:34:34,480 --> 00:34:36,440
No, no, no you cannot do this.

668
00:34:36,691 --> 00:34:39,360
- I won't allow it.
- It's not something you can stop.

669
00:34:39,485 --> 00:34:42,572
Try me. I am not without
resources, young man.

670
00:34:42,738 --> 00:34:44,907
"But he said he was gonna use
his own money for it."

671
00:34:45,950 --> 00:34:48,619
- "And then he said..."
- Time's on my side, Elspeth.

672
00:34:49,704 --> 00:34:51,289
What do you mean, Timothy?!

673
00:34:53,040 --> 00:34:54,625
Timothy, come back here!

674
00:34:55,293 --> 00:34:56,335
I knew what he meant.

675
00:34:56,460 --> 00:34:59,589
Hartley was going to wait until I was dead,
and then use my money

676
00:34:59,714 --> 00:35:03,050
and my daughter to turn the Cook name
into an international joke.

677
00:35:04,385 --> 00:35:06,971
So the next time he went to that place
he was always visiting

678
00:35:08,222 --> 00:35:09,265
we followed.

679
00:35:17,023 --> 00:35:20,735
- Why slit Hartley's throat?
- That was the telltale sign...

680
00:35:21,027 --> 00:35:23,821
A hunter's humanity, if you will.

681
00:35:24,530 --> 00:35:27,867
You learned how to hunt and kill
at a young age didn't you, Elspeth?

682
00:35:29,535 --> 00:35:30,745
Your father taught you.

683
00:35:32,330 --> 00:35:34,248
Yes. He was very firm on that point.

684
00:35:35,291 --> 00:35:36,834
"Never let the animal suffer."

685
00:35:38,461 --> 00:35:41,422
I got awfully cross with Consuela
for mislaying this.

686
00:35:43,382 --> 00:35:45,009
I shall have to apologize.

687
00:35:57,188 --> 00:35:58,981
Hey. What's up?

688
00:35:59,398 --> 00:36:00,608
There's something I have to
talk to you about.

689
00:36:00,733 --> 00:36:01,776
What's that?

690
00:36:02,985 --> 00:36:04,028
Wayne?

691
00:36:05,446 --> 00:36:06,489
What is it?

692
00:36:12,203 --> 00:36:14,955
A friend of mine is a ranger
at Vandermeer State Park

693
00:36:15,081 --> 00:36:17,917
and maybe I can get him to give
you a waiver to get married

694
00:36:18,042 --> 00:36:19,835
- at that Quaker meeting house.
- Really?

695
00:36:20,294 --> 00:36:22,630
Yeah. I think. I can try.

696
00:36:23,381 --> 00:36:25,091
Wayne, that's fantastic.

697
00:36:26,217 --> 00:36:27,635
- Thank you so much.
- Yeah.

698
00:36:27,927 --> 00:36:30,346
- I'm gonna call Craig.
- Yeah, okay.

699
00:36:41,315 --> 00:36:42,358
Please.

700
00:36:42,942 --> 00:36:45,277
- Thank you for coming by.
- Oh, it's no problem.

701
00:36:46,570 --> 00:36:48,906
Nice place. Tidy.

702
00:36:49,490 --> 00:36:50,533
Thank you.

703
00:36:50,866 --> 00:36:51,909
Please.

704
00:36:52,118 --> 00:36:54,662
I wanted to tell you
how much I appreciated

705
00:36:54,787 --> 00:36:58,249
your letting me come along
on your investigation.

706
00:36:58,374 --> 00:37:00,167
It was fun.

707
00:37:00,292 --> 00:37:02,044
Hmm, it was fun, wasn't it?

708
00:37:02,670 --> 00:37:03,796
That was my pleasure.

709
00:37:04,964 --> 00:37:06,757
- Thank you.
- Um, look...

710
00:37:08,843 --> 00:37:10,302
Won't beat around the bush.

711
00:37:11,679 --> 00:37:13,055
About me dying...

712
00:37:14,056 --> 00:37:16,517
I-I know what's going to happen now.

713
00:37:16,642 --> 00:37:18,144
I've seen it.

714
00:37:18,352 --> 00:37:19,645
There are no mysteries.

715
00:37:20,646 --> 00:37:21,939
It's going to get bad...

716
00:37:22,857 --> 00:37:23,941
very soon

717
00:37:24,859 --> 00:37:25,985
and then worse.

718
00:37:26,944 --> 00:37:30,364
And I have no interest
in letting nature take its course.

719
00:37:31,115 --> 00:37:34,160
- You understand?
- Uh, yes.

720
00:37:34,368 --> 00:37:38,038
- You, uh, you wanna kill yourself.
- In a nutshell.

721
00:37:40,291 --> 00:37:42,293
I have pills I can take.

722
00:37:42,877 --> 00:37:44,462
The problem is

723
00:37:45,838 --> 00:37:48,299
if there is an unexplained death

724
00:37:48,424 --> 00:37:51,761
if a body is found in an apartment

725
00:37:52,136 --> 00:37:55,097
